iguration committed in the log requires the other member.\\\"}]\nc2['knowledge']=[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"1a8ca5d0b10a4e248b1d2d93c8656a9e-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":3,\n  \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Used for why the understated membership lowers the quorum below the committed configuration's requirement, letting the leader accept an entry that only a minority of the committed voters holds.\\\"}]\nc3['knowledge']=[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"6420ecc11ae840028bf3e70220f5fd17-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":3,\n  \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Used to place the two observed operator paths within the recorded set of repair paths: RecoverCluster is one of them and live bootstrap is not.\\\"}]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('uses added:', sum(len(x.get('knowledge',[])) for x in d['interpretations']))\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
